ent-MobRotIntelligent = intelligent rot
    .desc = A rooted consciousness growing a colony through living tissue.
ent-RotIntelligentEye = colony eye
ent-RotTissue = colony tissue
    .desc = Living strands connecting the colony's organs. Severing them disables isolated structures.
ent-RotWall = organic wall
    .desc = An airtight barrier of woven cartilage, vulnerable to fire.
ent-RotOrganicDoor = organic valve
    .desc = A living passage that opens for rot creatures.
ent-RotEyeball = eyeball
    .desc = A watchful organ sharing its sight with the colony.
ent-RotFlagellum = flagellum
    .desc = A contractile tail that propels its grid. Its tip needs open space.
ent-RotKidney = kidney
    .desc = A pulsating organ that turns the colony's grid.
ent-RotProducer = progenitor
    .desc = A large digestive organ producing biomass while connected to the core.
ent-RotNursery = nursery
    .desc = Grows one random monster after two minutes of nourishment. Disconnection pauses growth.
ent-RotNutritionBlob = nutritious mass
    .desc = A nester's rich bolus. One full blob feeds two hungry larvae.
ent-RotRallyMarker = colony rally point
ent-MobRotNester = nester
    .desc = A one-eyed ghoul moving on all four limbs. Nutrition for larvae accumulates beneath its ribs.
ent-ActionRotIntelligentMenu = Colony
    .desc = Buildings, biomass, vision sources and unfinished growth.
ent-ActionRotIntelligentReturn = Return to core
ent-ActionRotIntelligentPilot = Pilot grid
    .desc = Open the shuttle interface. Use again to return control to the eye.
ent-ActionRotIntelligentUnanchor = Release grid anchor
    .desc = Release your grid, including a forcibly anchored station.
ent-ActionRotIntelligentBuild = Grow selected building
ent-ActionRotIntelligentRepair = Heal organ
    .desc = Heal up to 100 damage using biomass. Incoming damage interrupts healing.
ent-ActionRotIntelligentDissolve = Dissolve organ
    .desc = Dissolve your structure and recover part of its biomass cost.
ent-ActionRotIntelligentAdopt = Join creature to colony
    .desc = Adopt an unowned rot creature. Another living colony cannot be claimed.
ent-ActionRotIntelligentRally = Rally creatures
    .desc = Mark a rally point for nearby idle creatures for 30 seconds. Threats take priority.
ghost-role-rot-intelligent-name = Intelligent rot
ghost-role-rot-intelligent-description = Grow tissue and organs, see through your creatures and eyeballs, and turn your grid into a living ship.
ghost-role-rot-intelligent-rules = You are a team antagonist of rot. Protect your core and allied creatures. You cannot remotely operate ordinary doors or machinery. The colony loses control when its core dies.
rot-building-tissue = Tissue
rot-building-tissue-desc = Expand across existing floor by one adjacent tile. Connects organs to the core.
rot-building-wall = Wall
rot-building-wall-desc = An airtight barrier. Can gradually replace a destructible wall along the colony's edge.
rot-building-door = Valve
rot-building-door-desc = An airtight passage for rot. Can replace a wall.
rot-building-eyeball = Eyeball
rot-building-eyeball-desc = Vision up to 24 tiles. Opaque walls block sight; glass does not.
rot-building-flagellum = Flagellum
rot-building-flagellum-desc = A 1×3 engine. The arrow shows thrust direction. Its opposite end needs open space.
rot-building-kidney = Kidney
rot-building-kidney-desc = A 2×2 gyroscope. Turns the grid without electricity.
rot-building-producer = Progenitor
rot-building-producer-desc = A 3×3 organ. Produces 1 biomass per second while connected.
rot-building-nursery = Nursery
rot-building-nursery-desc = A 2×2 organ. After 120 seconds releases three carriers, one hungry, one sated or one nester with equal chances.
rot-intelligent-menu = Rot colony
rot-intelligent-buildings = Buildings
rot-intelligent-cameras = Vision
rot-intelligent-projects = Growth
rot-intelligent-command-return = Core
rot-intelligent-command-pilot = Pilot grid
rot-intelligent-command-unanchor = Release anchor
rot-intelligent-command-rotate = Rotate 90°
